    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with limited opportunities as most of our core offensive catalysts are sidelined by scheduled team off-days. With **Yordan Alvarez**, **Junior Caminero**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, and **Trea Turner** all inactive, the lineup depth is significantly tested. The focal point of today\u2019s rotation is **Chase Meidroth**, who anchors the infield at 43.40. While his position in the bottom third of the order against Parker Messick suppresses his scoring ceiling, **Chase Meidroth** benefits from a dynamic platoon advantage (L) that offsets the moderate 3.51 xERA of the opposing starter. We are closely monitoring the official lineup card; should **Chase Meidroth** move up from his projected 7-hole, we may see an incremental adjustment to his efficiency score.\n\nThe bench remains stagnant today due to the lack of available games, meaning no internal competition was required to determine the starting nine. Had the full roster been in action, **Christian Yelich** and **Caleb Durbin** would have been clear prioritize for their elite SB potential, a category we continue to over-index on given its scarcity in the current Roto landscape. As it stands, the risk profile for today is defined by the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Chase Meidroth** and the absence of high-upside secondary options like **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Christian Encarnacion-Strand**, **Colt Keith**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Josh Smith**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Carson Benge**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Pedro Ramirez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Jacob Gonzalez**. We are effectively in a preservation phase, awaiting the return of our primary producers to resume our push in the 5x5 standings.",
